    "resolved_from_fallback": false,
    "final_cot": "The image shows trapezoid ABCD, where AB is the lower base and CD is the upper base, the two are parallel; the labels give AB=52, CD=39, AD=5, BC=12. Using the coordinate/projection method, set A=(0,0), B=(52,0). Because CD is parallel to AB and CD=39, set D=(x,h), C=(x+39,h). From AD=5, get x^2+h^2=25. From BC=12, get (52-(x+39))^2+h^2=144, namely (13-x)^2+h^2=144. Subtract the two equations: [(13-x)^2+h^2]-(x^2+h^2)=144-25, so (13-x)^2-x^2=119. Expanding gives 169-26x=119, therefore x=25/13. Thus h^2=25-(25/13)^2=3600/169, so h=60/13. The area of the trapezoid is ((AB+CD)/2)h=((52+39)/2)(60/13)=210.",
