          "method_draft": "Construct a parallelogram-triangle decomposition. From C draw a segment CE parallel and equal to AD, meeting AB at E so that AECD is a parallelogram. Then AE=CD=39, so EB=AB-AE=52-39=13. Also CE=AD=5 and CB=12, so triangle CEB has side lengths 5, 12, and 13; it is a right triangle. Its area is (1/2)(5)(12)=30, so the altitude from C to EB is 2*30/13=60/13. This altitude is the trapezoid height. Then area of ABCD is ((52+39)/2)(60/13)=210.",
